{"repositoryId":651431082,"availability":"available","full":"shakfu/gen-dsp","name":"gen-dsp","description":"gen-dsp converts code exported from a Max gen~ object and a graph-oriented dsl into multiple dsp plugin architectures.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":20,"forks":3,"created":"2023-06-09T08:14:01Z","updated":"2026-10-13T06:14:28Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://shakfu.github.io/gen-dsp/","topics":["dsp","gen","maxmsp","puredata","python3"],"demo":"https://shakfu.github.io/gen-dsp/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:31.881Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:31.881Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:31.881Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T06:39:31.881Z","stars":20,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The 17 targets are PureData, Max/MSP, ChucK, AudioUnit (AUv2), AUv3, CLAP, VST3, LV2, SuperCollider, VCV Rack, Daisy, Circle, Percussa SSP, Web Audio (WASM), Standalone (miniaudio), Csound, and nice-plug (a Rust CLAP/VST3 crate) -- spanning desktop plugin formats, embedded firmware, and the browser.","This project is a friendly fork of Michael Spears' genext which was originally created to \"compile code exported from a Max gen object into an \"external\" object that can be loaded into a PureData patch.\""],"features":["Each parameter becomes a captioned fader carrying two bindings: an OSC address /myeffect/ whose argument is scaled into the parameter's declared range (a room-size parameter over [0.1, 300] sends 150, not a bare 0.5),…","The generated plugins do not speak OSC themselves, so for the two backends that can receive it without new C++ the receiving half is generated too: a playable Pd patch wired from netreceive/oscparse into the external,…","Buffer names must be valid C identifiers (alphanumeric, starting with a letter)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shakfu/gen-dsp/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ad321cba20